<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Argishti II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 714–685 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century-bce">8th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Argishti II was king of Urartu from about 714 to 685 BCE, succeeding his father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rusa-i">Rusa I</a> after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sargon-ii">Sargon II</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assyrian-empire">Assyria</a>'s devastating campaign of 714 BCE. He restored royal authority and campaigned to the east, leaving inscriptions as far as the region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-urmia">Lake Urmia</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mount-ararat">Ararat</a> plain, but he avoided direct conflict with Assyria.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/argishti-ii.jpg" alt="Argishti II" width="320" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Beko · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cuneiform_inscription_of_Urartian_King_Argishti_II.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
